{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791594493,"nonce":"dM+3PZswSAqdFhlGx3yK23DH7i4=","title":"Land the blinc_abi css-paint branch, then point the addon back at blinc_abi","message":"CSS paint is now read in Rust by blinc_abi and applied by the addon (see 6e33649). The blinc_abi side is on branch css-paint in the worktree /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/blinc_abi-paint, cut from main at 3db5b2d, with nothing committed yet. Until it lands, native/Cargo.toml points at ../../blinc_abi-paint.\n\nWhat blocks committing the blinc_ts side\n- CI checks blinc_abi out at a pinned commit into deps/blinc_abi, so the path to the worktree cannot be committed. Land the branch first, move the CI pin to the landed commit, and put the path back to ../../blinc_abi.\n- Landing is a rebase onto main and a fast-forward, per the agent that owns main in blinc_abi, who stages by explicit path. That agent wants the commit id once it lands: its HashLink SDK switches to these parsers (its issue a1b9d37).\n\nWhat the branch changes in blinc_abi\n- New under src/css: color, gradient, transform, filter, shadow, border, quantity and paint (paint_writes, is_paint_property, PaintWrite, PaintUnits), with tests_paint. css/ still builds with --no-default-features --features css-cli.\n- styled.rs: restyle reads each node's paint into typed writes, with unsets, behind Styles::set_paint_output (off by default, so a host that draws from resolved declarations is untouched), take_paint and repaint.\n- layout.rs: the border and per-side border shorthands, border-style, and thin, medium and thick border widths.\n- types.rs: Debug on GlassEffects.\n\nChecked: blinc_abi css tests 57, the scene suite 85, and the default-features HashLink build; blinc_ts 34 unit tests, 23 windowless native suites and the adapters. The window tests were not run.\n\nAcceptance: blinc_abi main has the branch; CI pins it; native/Cargo.toml is back to ../../blinc_abi; the suites above pass on CI.","files":null}]}